From dcc04d60e986d574825c2a0d9239b2cd4a685b87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: djnice <djnice@freemail.hu>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 10:06:20 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] audiotrack: "native" device, PCM at the source's sample rate
 on Dune HD boxes

A new output device, "native": as "pcm", but a mono or stereo PCM source
at 32, 44.1, 96 or 192 kHz goes out at its own rate, 16-bit stereo, where
the box sends such PCM to HDMI as it is, instead of being resampled to the
output's mixer rate (48 kHz) - for a music player.

The Dune HD Android firmware (ro.dunehd.native_sr=1) has an attribute flag
for it, 0x4000 (AudioAttributes, no name there but in its FLAG_ALL_PUBLIC):
its audio policy gives such a track a direct output (DIRECT | DEEP_BUFFER,
the Amlogic HAL's PCM_DIRECT) at the track's rate. Measured on a Dune HD
Pro 8K Plus (Android 11, S928X): 44.1, 96 and 192 kHz on
HDMI (amhdmitx config, ALSA pcm5p) from an app's AudioTrack; without the
flag the mixer's 48 kHz, FLAG_HW_AV_SYNC also 48 kHz (the HAL mixes the
hw-sync LPCM). The Dune's own player asks for 0x4e00.

The AudioTrack is made from AudioAttributes and AudioFormat (API 21) with
the flag. Not used: on another box, when persist.dunehd.native_sr.disable
is true, above persist.dunehd.native_sr.max_sr, for a rate the direct
output does not list (88.2, 176.4 kHz: the mixer's way) or the HDMI sink's
EDID (Amlogic aud_cap) does not take, for 48 kHz (the mixer's own rate) and
for more than 2 channels. If the AudioTrack cannot be made, the output's
rate as before. The output info file says "pcm 44100 2 native".

Message-Id: <20261108-dvfel-audiotrack-native-rate@djnice>

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
